LaunchUnitConcreteTest
├── When the pool launcher token is whitelisted
│   └── It should revert with {InvalidPoolLauncherToken}
└── When the pool launcher token is not whitelisted
    ├── When the pool has already been created
    │   └── It should revert with {PoolAlreadyExists}
    └── When the pool has not been created yet
        ├── When the tokenToPair is not whitelisted
        │   └── It should revert with {InvalidToken}
        └── When the tokenToPair is whitelisted
            ├── When the refund address is the zero address
            │   └── It should revert with {InvalidRefundAddress}
            └── When the refund address is not the zero address 
                ├── When the balance of poolLauncherToken of the sender is lower than amountPoolLauncherToken
                │   └── It should revert with {ERC20InsufficientBalance}
                └── When the balance of poolLauncherToken of the sender is higher or equal to amountPoolLauncherToken
                    ├── When the balance of tokenToPair of the sender is lower than amountTokenToPair
                    │   └── It should revert with {ERC20InsufficientBalance}
                    └── When the balance of tokenToPair of the sender is higher or equal to amountTokenToPair
                        ├── When the amounts deposited are smaller than the min amounts
                        │   └── It should revert with {InsufficientAmount}
                        └── When the amounts deposited are greater than or equal to the min amounts
                            ├── When lock duration is zero
                            │   ├── It should create a new pool launcher pool
                            │   ├── It should return any seed liquidity to the recipient
                            │   ├── It should refund any leftover tokens to the user
                            │   ├── It should map the pool launcher token to the new pool
                            │   ├── It should store the info for the new pool in storage
                            │   └── It should emit a {Launch} event
                            ├── When lock duration is not zero or UINT32_MAX
                            │   ├── It should create a new pool launcher pool
                            │   ├── It should lock the seed liquidity in a new Locker for the given duration
                            │   ├── It should refund any leftover tokens to the user
                            │   ├── It should map the pool launcher token to the new pool
                            │   ├── It should store the info for the new pool in storage
                            │   └── It should emit a {Launch} event
                            └── When lock duration is UINT32_MAX
                                ├── It should create a new pool launcher pool
                                ├── It should permanently lock the seed liquidity in a new Locker
                                ├── It should refund any leftover tokens to the user
                                ├── It should map the pool launcher token to the new pool
                                ├── It should store the info for the new pool in storage
                                └── It should emit a {Launch} event
